  "notes": "{会合|かいごう} refers to gatherings or meetings, often more formal than casual get-togethers.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {会合|かいごう}を{開|ひら}く (to hold a meeting)\n- {会合|かいごう}に{出席|しゅっせき}する (to attend a meeting)\n- {会合|かいごう}を{設|もう}ける (to arrange a meeting)\n\nTYPES:\n- {定期|ていき}{会合|かいごう} (regular meeting)\n- {緊急|きんきゅう}{会合|かいごう} (emergency meeting)\n- {秘密|ひみつ}{会合|かいごう} (secret meeting)\n\nNUANCE:\n- More formal than {集|あつ}まり (gathering)\n- Less formal than {会議|かいぎ} (conference)\n- Often implies a purpose or agenda\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {会議|かいぎ}: meeting, conference (business)\n- {集会|しゅうかい}: assembly, gathering\n- {集|あつ}まり: gathering (casual)",
